From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: retain one removal per registered transport

Port the reviewed project correction from aba749b to the signed Linux 7.3
source. Retain Linux GPL attribution and the exact native APIs. The old
7.2.12 result did not establish inclusion in this patch queue.

Compared with Uke OEM 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd, OnePlus
fc892483f1d61f245924681eb5abd563564d9cba and Palawan
0d9f7fdf720ae9f4ecfbee4fadaf1e3b5c442e95. Source/host checks do not
qualify CDSP firmware startup, DMA quiescence or physical compute.

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c
@@ -226,7 +226,8 @@
 {
 	struct qcom_rproc_glink *glink = to_glink_subdev(subdev);
 
-	qcom_glink_smem_unregister(glink->edge);
+	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(glink->edge))
+		qcom_glink_smem_unregister(glink->edge);
 	glink->edge = NULL;
 }
 
@@ -339,7 +340,8 @@
 {
 	struct qcom_rproc_subdev *smd = to_smd_subdev(subdev);
 
-	qcom_smd_unregister_edge(smd->edge);
+	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(smd->edge))
+		qcom_smd_unregister_edge(smd->edge);
 	smd->edge = NULL;
 }
 
